# /usr/local/etc/otter/isolation-check.args on an Otter node (#122).
# Install mode 0600, root. The isolation check's options, one or two words a
# line (scripts/isolation-check.sh documents them); this node's private
# targets stay here, out of the repository. With no file, the check runs
# with its defaults: the first node's addresses and no control plane.
#
# The control plane of the minimum profile is on this node:
-c
# Targets no jail may reach, host:port, where something listens:
#-t <the node's LAN address>:22
#-t <the LAN gateway>:80
# Non-Otter jails on this node, which must not reach the tenants:
#-n <jail>
